# Every value here is OPTIONAL public client configuration.
# An absent value disables its feature quietly; the app opens either way.
# 🔴 No server secret belongs in a VITE_ variable - the bundler inlines it.

# Telemetry is on by default when a destination is configured; there is no
# per-user switch. A development build sends nothing (D54). The desktop bundle
# carries only public identifiers and a public GA4 broker enable flag.
# [OPTIONAL] Enable GA4 only after analytics-ingest is deployed with server-side
# GA4_MEASUREMENT_ID and GA4_MP_API_SECRET. No secret enters a VITE_ variable.
VITE_GA4_INGEST_ENABLED=
# [OPTIONAL] Bundled Amplitude event destination.
VITE_AMPLITUDE_API_KEY=
# [OPTIONAL] Bundled Sentry crash destination.
VITE_SENTRY_DSN=
# Supabase - the backend, since 2026-09-05. Both values come from the FilesHub
# vault; the publishable key is PUBLIC by design and its whole security model is
# RLS. 🔴 The secret key belongs nowhere near this file.
#
# The project exists and its schema is applied (ref nlmetjyytgwaxcliusuo, created
# 2026-09-07), and Google - the only sign-in this app offers - is enabled on it:
# `GET /auth/v1/settings` reports `external.google: true` (MANUAL-TASKS row 15,
# 2026-09-24). The app never sees the Google client's id or secret; they live in
# Supabase's own Auth -> Providers form.
#
# 🔴 Fill these two in a LOCAL `.env` only to verify sign-in and sync on a dev
#    build. `configuredFeatures()` turns both on whenever the two are present and
#    asks no provider, so an empty pair is the honest signed-out build. Release
#    builds get them from the repository variables, which `desktop-release.yml`
#    exports only when `SUPABASE_ENABLED` is `true` (set 2026-09-25, O6') and only
#    after probing that the project still answers `external.google: true`.
#
# Signed out, every cleanup feature works as before, and the engine makes no
# network calls at all.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
